# Medium-object churn: every round rebuilds a 1,000-element set, whose
# storage spans many lines but less than a block. The loop forces the set
# each round, so only one set is live at a time and the heap should not
# grow with the number of rounds.
rounds: 32000
churn(s, i): s set.remove(i % 1000) set.add(i % 1000)
done?(s, i): (i = rounds) ∨ ((s set.size) < 0)
loop(s, i): done?(s, i) then(s, loop(churn(s, i), i + 1))
r: loop(range(0, 1000) set.from-list, 0) set.size
